#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078433 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6ae15d-7005-5a93-9432-c4814dc9573d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given the Pattern and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062e60e2-b046-5229-9c39-d03fb085f197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333043} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2613c6-effa-59ac-a0c2-64eb7eab0c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333585} {:answer/id #uuid "9170b646-bdd2-5f36-8131-6194a410f909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334287} {:answer/id #uuid "acb563d8-4a7f-5f8b-8f93-2053052c13aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334506} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc3343a-f031-5d99-84b3-6ce60bd0ec30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f2613c6-effa-59ac-a0c2-64eb7eab0c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333585} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d768c5-7f47-526a-9f4a-7e5a3245070c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "603329e3-3f7e-5367-af27-44144e5341b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-67075" :question/problem "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n7+21+35+…=175\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\\,\\,\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=175$, and the first term ${a}_{1}=7.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =21-7 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 175 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 7+(N-1)\\cdot 14) \\\\ 175 & =\\frac{N}{2}(14+14N-14) \\\\ 175 & =\\frac{N}{2}(14N) \\\\ 175 & =7{N}^{2} \\\\ 25 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$can't be negative. Therefore, our series has $N=5$ terms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d2d8b48-e9ad-5cb8-8343-f72fa96ebb8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({2}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333250} {:answer/id #uuid "5c445d43-e33b-5c23-b1df-193662f6a0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(1-{2}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333829} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc1d657-6a01-5021-b0f9-bfb570e9b10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334394} {:answer/id #uuid "f607b3a4-4d6a-59d0-8288-b410ddc4f463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335146} {:answer/id #uuid "fb318f93-3091-5697-b877-1ca949a2a4c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1-{4}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f607b3a4-4d6a-59d0-8288-b410ddc4f463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{N}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335146} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a67d07-89d8-5add-92e3-c98fc2357074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09e81789-ed75-5f91-be45-fe9e5d6bad8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-67090" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $4$ and the common ratio is $2?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 4 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {2}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 4 & =4{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=1$ and $r=2.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{1(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & ={2}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e807c1b4-ec12-578e-adfe-38f82bc92701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368630} {:answer/id #uuid "12e80468-7314-5375-a06c-ac6bbe01fde3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368631} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4fa272-e3a0-5a72-966e-a6949699eb99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368632} {:answer/id #uuid "bbab7461-db2d-5d59-b338-baad2f7e5541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368633} {:answer/id #uuid "584d0dc4-bafb-53d6-8b06-244aa54043ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12e80468-7314-5375-a06c-ac6bbe01fde3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368631} :answer-field/id #uuid "6802ba7f-a62f-596f-82ab-3508a6bdc4ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c3b2996-4d45-5fac-b139-960f69bf9ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-6730" :question/problem "![](images/94/9434dda63c08fc1202d16ab5410fe7061050515876ffa473d8720db39079af3e.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}+{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2t}{3{t}^{2}+2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3t+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=2,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2}{3(2)+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a00fa7-a425-5b28-941c-bc8027676ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Convergence of a Geometric Series With an Arbitrary Starting Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "350e836a-d347-540c-8c04-df66db7b36da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is convergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333476} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb719ab-a22a-56ab-b42c-a89d8cd8e9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent because $|r|\\le 1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333685} {:answer/id #uuid "943c7188-2b1c-5397-8a91-d08c229b0c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334310} {:answer/id #uuid "d67812a4-47f6-5477-ae0d-6c61a7dacb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Inconclusive because $|r|=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334867} {:answer/id #uuid "e608f853-98f4-5fc1-8300-895e9efcd360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is convergent because $|r|<1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "943c7188-2b1c-5397-8a91-d08c229b0c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334310} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b96fa8c-b11c-56f0-bb9a-174f0a700a1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "860416f7-74aa-5f00-b916-8a018898ec49" :question/math-academy-id "q-67458" :question/problem "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series  ${\\sum }_{n=3}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{5}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{n+1}$ ?" :question/worked-solution "The series starts with $n=3.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{{a}_{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{5}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4+1}}{\\frac{3}{5}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{5}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43dcbb7e-ba21-506f-a706-bfb28371e0a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term Smaller Than a Given Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d288ec97-97c9-55c4-8fe2-1bdeaaadd156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $18$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334829} {:answer/id #uuid "d71e6adc-6bff-595d-9d94-13225d9cea6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $15$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334875} {:answer/id #uuid "da81e9ee-4a30-5d03-b828-3480b90a4b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $19$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334903} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5fae1a-806a-561a-9570-394a7f222bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $17$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335070} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8c5c2c-fa19-57ba-8c16-3c4f14b18fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $16$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d288ec97-97c9-55c4-8fe2-1bdeaaadd156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $18$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334829} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6de6a63-6358-59d8-9d9c-7fdba98debf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96f03ca4-722a-50b8-895c-e2999102c436" :question/math-academy-id "q-67493" :question/problem "What is the first term that is less than $0.000\\,6$ in the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n64,\\,32,\\,16,\\,8,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=64$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{32}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $n$th term of the sequence can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={2}^{6}\\cdot {2}^{1-n} \\\\  & ={2}^{7-n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want the $n$th term to be less than $0.000\\,6.$\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & <0.000\\,6 \\\\ {2}^{7-n} & <0.000\\,6 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡{(2)}^{7-n} & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6) \\\\ (7-n)\\operatorname{log}⁡(2) & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6) \\\\ 7-n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)} \\\\ -n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}-7 \\\\ n & >7-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEstimating the right-hand side using a calculator, we get:\n\n$$\n7-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}≈17.703\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $18$th term is the first term of the sequence that is less than $0.000\\,6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c8f1095-0b60-5dad-8471-4efa453e9d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the First Term Is Unknown"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31f79c15-e015-58ee-9759-1651faf25e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $10$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333447} {:answer/id #uuid "398d4c7a-0785-51dd-a6f3-ad5515ef3183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $12$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333527} {:answer/id #uuid "45ca5716-9eb2-586f-a070-fc824e9589a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $13$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333633} {:answer/id #uuid "56d76ff2-b484-54dd-a935-e81f1b63a229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $11$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333775} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e570b2-ef64-5bdf-9d62-b47beca6903d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $14$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "398d4c7a-0785-51dd-a6f3-ad5515ef3183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $12$th term" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333527} :answer-field/id #uuid "e85b7624-09f8-51bb-bb59-2a37f079db87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5456760-9cdb-54e3-82ce-b6d6e704f8ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-67516" :question/problem "The $6$th term of a geometric sequence is $3$, and the common ratio is $3.$ What is the first term of this sequence to exceed\n$907?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that ${a}_{6}=3$ and  $r=3$, we can use the $n$th term formula to solve for ${a}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{6-1} \\\\ 3 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{3}^{4}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{81}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $n$th term of the geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={3}^{-4}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={3}^{n-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want $n$th term to be greater than $907.$\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{n-5} & >907 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡{(3)}^{n-5} & >\\operatorname{log}⁡(907) \\\\ (n-5)\\operatorname{log}⁡(3) & >\\operatorname{log}⁡(907) \\\\ n-5 & >\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(907)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\ n & >\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(907)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEstimating the right-hand side using a calculator, we get:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(907)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}+5≈11.199\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12$th term is the first term of the sequence that exceeds $907.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89b9224-71e0-5c90-8e9e-5fc3f7e29574" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit of a Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a8dc82-7cf5-5eb6-9cb4-cc65873162f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332994} {:answer/id #uuid "23067ab0-a97b-578d-a7f6-922c5560af95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333309} {:answer/id #uuid "278eaf18-ae13-5c80-9f73-65a7c5851538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333352} {:answer/id #uuid "a86c9c11-9f5f-5f47-aba6-0a4fa214e750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334465} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6faae3-0ba2-5019-bc97-30d25878672c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6faae3-0ba2-5019-bc97-30d25878672c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335071} :answer-field/id #uuid "74920e33-2331-55ac-ad49-1862b5802327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "683cbe5d-f5f2-5d3d-bddd-bb767f5e130a" :question/math-academy-id "q-67609" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f71a8f16-93d4-5e5a-9b8b-e29efc682430" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reflection of a Cosine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91aa4299-8622-56c9-9965-0d314906b5fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403260} {:answer/id #uuid "7651d643-52d0-5fbc-a55d-9c2d891d4dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=cos⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403261} {:answer/id #uuid "f54912f6-668c-587e-a31b-1ebd55260469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403262} {:answer/id #uuid "67c9f2ed-6bc9-5306-bbd4-92c22c1a12b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403263} {:answer/id #uuid "b68c49b7-6a46-50a7-8650-9997f0344c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x+1)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54912f6-668c-587e-a31b-1ebd55260469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403262} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc78750f-325d-5b2a-a8a4-508033a97f08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4668d94d-a174-5c1d-bde7-38ebd0634499" :question/math-academy-id "q-6761" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d660b71abd6c03c817b6cf18c5320a3f27d4fbf650f1ea032d27bf1652d3066.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/86/867ec8135efc671ea26c6691a9aef4803c35179b86b7af3b605c4b7d1d3a2498.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115370 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Using Direct Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b11084-dd01-56d4-aa91-3866966fdea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333052} {:answer/id #uuid "35947c74-7f98-5be2-8992-082e0574bb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333483} {:answer/id #uuid "403c2239-1d05-57d4-84ba-bc9be2040036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333597} {:answer/id #uuid "58d2768d-4e1a-5fc0-a198-6a919d796e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333800} {:answer/id #uuid "70ddd71e-86f5-5b19-b3be-970625ec51d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ddd71e-86f5-5b19-b3be-970625ec51d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334017} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15b75bc-2eb6-5cae-9c24-0d804ed0aea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21413485-e217-53bf-aba0-585e7743ce88" :question/math-academy-id "q-67625" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{4}^{x}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{x}}=2$, what is the value of constant $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{4}^{x}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{x}} & =\\frac{{4}^{0}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-c}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $2,$ we can equate the above with $2,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-c}{3} & =2 \\\\ 1-c & =6 \\\\ -c & =6-1 \\\\ c & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10100e89-21d6-53c5-a7de-f14fd73ce4b7" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Different Rules to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3e5e428-55c6-547c-8a43-b717c453f470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403267} {:answer/id #uuid "5a425311-e469-5ff8-a1bd-9454c87692d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403268} {:answer/id #uuid "deefb1bd-abfc-5373-b490-cefccc51642f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403269} {:answer/id #uuid "35d21c38-0370-5025-8bcc-f844ea185348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403270} {:answer/id #uuid "934c6624-2691-5291-bbc2-1f43189f8e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deefb1bd-abfc-5373-b490-cefccc51642f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403269} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a133e4-dd1e-5f83-ae36-ea8f3bd624c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c978569-5523-50ca-8c37-1ccfd41ba3f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-67703" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b0074bb582011695cec9807beab1623c6aab894e0c6abeb1bf3068be6ed3543.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}f(x)=9.$ \n\nApplying the root rule, we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}(25-f(x))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{25-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a76efbd-cefd-5aa0-953e-8ab50bec7ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height Corresponding to an Extended Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f70c953-efc1-574d-8fb8-f485df44a32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/109606d69a47d93c20b57ba740c8fec43164f0b71137e805a11cf8fd78cc3e5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392954} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0a8ba2-53f6-517e-9751-d2499c8bbd45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf634d9c8c1a307a3fdc892ca5e21745dc58d073a2b6f57b62146eaeca4697e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392955} {:answer/id #uuid "784b392f-7bf7-5c31-b3ae-c517fa954657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/decfd00e92564ee5b585db65f9c0e7939c870f25d6abe8127caf68744a9bab71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392956} {:answer/id #uuid "7c36a4eb-a024-58d0-8ed7-0ada2ed0db01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d2dd7694f1a3270b8828c6d70c54aae70fa4278080d51e221bd381118fdc6bea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392957} {:answer/id #uuid "37876aac-ef37-5759-be7